Task 1: Configure Red Hat Insights for Automatic Remediation
Subtask 1.1: Install and Register Insights Client
First, we'll install the Red Hat Insights client and register the system.

Update the system packages:
sudo dnf update -y
Install the insights-client package:
sudo dnf install -y insights-client
Register the system with Red Hat Insights:
sudo insights-client --register
Verify the registration:
sudo insights-client --status
Expected output should show the system is registered and connected.

Subtask 1.2: Configure Insights Client Settings
Create a custom configuration file:
sudo cp /etc/insights-client/insights-client.conf /etc/insights-client/insights-client.conf.backup
Edit the configuration file:
sudo nano /etc/insights-client/insights-client.conf
Add the following configuration settings:
[insights-client]
# Enable automatic updates
auto_config=True
# Set collection schedule
cron_schedule=0 2 * * *
# Enable remediation
remediation=True
# Log level for debugging
loglevel=INFO
Restart the insights-client service:
sudo systemctl restart insights-client
sudo systemctl enable insights-client
Subtask 1.3: Set Up Automated Data Collection
Create a systemd timer for regular insights collection:
sudo nano /etc/systemd/system/insights-collection.timer
Add the timer configuration:
[Unit]
Description=Red Hat Insights Collection Timer
Requires=insights-collection.service

[Timer]
OnCalendar=daily
Persistent=true
RandomizedDelaySec=3600

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
Create the corresponding service file:
sudo nano /etc/systemd/system/insights-collection.service
Add the service configuration:
[Unit]
Description=Red Hat Insights Collection Service
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/bin/insights-client
User=root
StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal
Enable and start the timer:
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable insights-collection.timer
sudo systemctl start insights-collection.timer
Verify the timer is active:
sudo systemctl list-timers insights-collection.timer
Task 2: Set Up Automated Patching and Updates via Insights
Subtask 2.1: Install and Configure DNF Automatic
Install dnf-automatic package:
sudo dnf install -y dnf-automatic
Configure dnf-automatic for security updates:
sudo nano /etc/dnf/automatic.conf
Modify the configuration:
[commands]
upgrade_type = security
random_sleep = 3600
network_online_timeout = 60
download_updates = yes
apply_updates = yes

[emitters]
emit_via = stdio
system_name = None

[command_email]
email_from = root@localhost
email_to = admin@localhost
email_host = localhost

[base]
debuglevel = 1
Enable and start dnf-automatic timer:
sudo systemctl enable --now dnf-automatic.timer
Subtask 2.2: Create Insights-Based Remediation Script
Create a remediation script directory:
sudo mkdir -p /opt/insights-remediation
Create the main remediation script:
sudo nano /opt/insights-remediation/auto-remediate.sh
Add the remediation script content:
#!/bin/bash

# Red Hat Insights Automated Remediation Script
# This script processes Insights recommendations and applies safe remediations

LOG_FILE="/var/log/insights-remediation.log"
INSIGHTS_DATA_DIR="/var/lib/insights"

# Function to log messages
log_message() {
    echo "$(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S') - $1" | tee -a "$LOG_FILE"
}

# Function to check if system is registered with Insights
check_insights_registration() {
    if insights-client --status | grep -q "Successfully registered"; then
        log_message "System is registered with Red Hat Insights"
        return 0
    else
        log_message "ERROR: System is not registered with Red Hat Insights"
        return 1
    fi
}

# Function to collect latest insights data
collect_insights_data() {
    log_message "Collecting latest Insights data..."
    if insights-client; then
        log_message "Insights data collection completed successfully"
        return 0
    else
        log_message "ERROR: Failed to collect Insights data"
        return 1
    fi
}

# Function to apply security updates
apply_security_updates() {
    log_message "Checking for security updates..."
    
    # Get list of security updates
    SECURITY_UPDATES=$(dnf --security check-update 2>/dev/null | grep -v "^$" | wc -l)
    
    if [ "$SECURITY_UPDATES" -gt 0 ]; then
        log_message "Found $SECURITY_UPDATES security updates. Applying..."
        
        # Apply security updates
        if dnf -y --security update; then
            log_message "Security updates applied successfully"
            
            # Check if reboot is required
            if needs-restarting -r; then
                log_message "System reboot required after updates"
                # Schedule reboot for maintenance window (2 AM)
                echo "shutdown -r +60 'System reboot for security updates'" | at now + 1 minute 2>/dev/null || true
            fi
        else
            log_message "ERROR: Failed to apply security updates"
            return 1
        fi
    else
        log_message "No security updates available"
    fi
}

# Function to fix common configuration issues
fix_configuration_issues() {
    log_message "Checking for common configuration issues..."
    
    # Fix SSH configuration issues
    if [ -f /etc/ssh/sshd_config ]; then
        # Ensure SSH root login is properly configured
        if grep -q "^PermitRootLogin yes" /etc/ssh/sshd_config; then
            log_message "WARNING: Root login via SSH is enabled"
            # Uncomment the next line to automatically disable root login
            # sed -i 's/^PermitRootLogin yes/PermitRootLogin no/' /etc/ssh/sshd_config
        fi
        
        # Ensure SSH protocol version 2 is used
        if ! grep -q "^Protocol 2" /etc/ssh/sshd_config; then
            echo "Protocol 2" >> /etc/ssh/sshd_config
            log_message "Added Protocol 2 to SSH configuration"
            systemctl reload sshd
        fi
    fi
    
    # Fix file permissions on sensitive files
    chmod 600 /etc/ssh/ssh_host_*_key 2>/dev/null || true
    chmod 644 /etc/ssh/ssh_host_*_key.pub 2>/dev/null || true
    
    log_message "Configuration checks completed"
}

# Function to update system packages based on Insights recommendations
update_packages() {
    log_message "Updating packages based on Insights recommendations..."
    
    # Update all packages (can be modified to be more selective)
    if dnf -y update; then
        log_message "Package updates completed successfully"
    else
        log_message "ERROR: Package update failed"
        return 1
    fi
}

# Main execution
main() {
    log_message "Starting Insights automated remediation process"
    
    # Check prerequisites
    if ! check_insights_registration; then
        exit 1
    fi
    
    # Collect latest data
    if ! collect_insights_data; then
        exit 1
    fi
    
    # Apply remediations
    apply_security_updates
    fix_configuration_issues
    
    log_message "Insights automated remediation process completed"
}

# Execute main function
main "$@"
Make the script executable:
sudo chmod +x /opt/insights-remediation/auto-remediate.sh
